From d13e78d57054dd380e40913c23d2b291ef8ab61a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Bodenham <matthew@bodenham.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:16:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] hw/mips: add X1600E machine for HiBy R1 bring-up (Tier C)

Local device model for booting the stock HiBy R1 v1.6 kernel
(unmodified xImage, decompressed to vmlinux.bin) inside QEMU as the
project's regression gate. Trace-driven: every block present is pinned
to a stock-kernel boot stop (docs/M1-bringup-log.md in the host repo).

- XBurstR2 CPU, 64 MiB DDR at 0, kernel loaded at phys 0x10000 with
  boot PC = the real kernel_entry (0x80585c60, head.S), SPL-style fw
  args table (argc=2, argv[1]=cmdline incl. mem=64M) at 0xA00000.
- UART0 at 0x10030000 (regshift 2; SCR seeded 0xa9 for the early-uart
  probe), INTC/TCU/RTC/pinctrl/UART1-3/PDMA/MSC0 zero-return stubs at
  the stock-DTB sizes, TCSM0 as plain RAM (0x134F0000).
- OST clockevent at 0x12000000: CPU IRQ line 4, +0x14 compare arm with
  vendor periodic auto-reload, +0x0C ack, and a free-running 1.5 MHz
  counter at 0x20/0x24 driven by the virtual clock (udelay/sched_clock
  depend on it advancing).
